Personal test build of the Deluge community firmware with three added
features. Based on `release/1.3` (commit `7ed25ad`). Source: branch
`arlo-fugue` in this repository.

**This is experimental.** Back up your SD card and keep your current
firmware file so you can go back.

## Install

1. Copy `deluge-arlo-v12-fugue-v5.bin` to the root of the SD card
   (remove any other `.bin` there).
2. Hold SHIFT while switching the Deluge on.
3. Settings > Community Features: switch on what you want to try.
   All three are off by default.

| 7-seg | OLED               |
|-------|--------------------|
| FUGU  | Fugue              |
| ARLO  | Arranger Loop      |
| ARFX  | Arranger Loop 2+FX |

## Arranger Loop (ARLO)

A loop lane below the last track in arranger view. Yellow is the loop,
the green pad is its start (A), the red pad its end (B). Playback wraps
from B to A without stopping.

- Set a marker: tap it (it blinks), then tap where it should go.
- Loop on/off: the lane's mute pad.
- Hold a loop pad + PLAY: start from A.
- Hold a loop pad + turn `<>`: move the whole loop.
- Hold a loop pad + tap outside the loop: jump by the loop's length.
- Grid view: a yellow sidebar pad switches from the playing clips into
  the looped arrangement when the clips finish.
- Loop points are saved with the song.

## Arranger Loop 2+FX (ARFX, needs ARLO)

A second, purple loop lane with its own set of 25 song FX values
(filters, delay, reverb, EQ, bitcrush, mod FX, volume, pan and more).

- The purple loop follows the yellow one until you move it. Only one
  loop is on at a time.
- Hold the purple body: its FX are heard. Let go: back to the song's.
  While held, the gold knobs edit purple's values.
- SHIFT + tap purple: latch. Hold purple + BACK: reset its FX.
- Fade in: hold green + press red (over the loop), or the 1st to 4th
  pad to its right (1 to 4 bars).
- Fade out: the same from the red pad, towards the left.
- SHIFT + a fade gesture: the fade latches and repeats on every pass.

## Fugue (FUGU)

A new entry in the clip menu, after Arpeggiator and Randomizer. It
copies the clip's notes into three more voices, each one transformed.
For synth, MIDI and CV clips, not kits.

Menu: `DEST`, `VOI2`, `VOI3`, `VOI4`, `RAND`, `APPL`

- `DEST`: `CLIP` writes the next three clips of the same track,
  `TRAC` writes three cloned tracks, `BOTH` fills a 4x4 block with
  slight variants.
- Per voice: on, pitch (scale-aware), octave, invert, direction,
  rotate, tempo (1/8 to 8), resolution; arp mode, sync, gate, rhythm;
  randomizer lock, note probability, velocity spread, bass probability.
- `RAND` rolls moderate values for all voices.
- `APPL` writes the voices. It asks `OVER` before replacing clips that
  already hold notes.

## Known limits and test status

- Fugue: no undo, Apply clears the undo history. Automation and MPE
  are not copied.
- Tested on hardware, mainly on a 7-segment Deluge and also on an OLED
  model: about 30 minutes of use without issues.
- The purple loop's FX (hold, latch, fades) work, but are still a bit
  unintuitive and rough around the edges.
- The wider Fugue tempo range (1/8 to 8) is new in this build and has
  not been on hardware yet.
- One freeze happened in earlier testing; the cause is not found.

Feedback is welcome, please open an issue here.
